5. A12 — Intent Envelope

5.1 Required contents

A conforming Intent Envelope MUST contain:

· (a) goal — the objective, in machine-readable form.
· (b) constraints — max price, merchant allowlist, deadline, and any domain-specific constraints.
· (c) envelope — spend cap and authorized action classes.
· (d) delegation — agent identifier, expiry, revocation status.
· (e) revocation endpoint — a reachable URL.

5.2 Delegation semantics

The envelope MUST be signed by the user. The agent MUST NOT hold raw user credentials. Every action taken by the agent MUST be traceable to an envelope clause. An action that is not traceable to an envelope clause MUST produce 0x-AMBIG-INTENT and MUST NOT commit.

5.3 Revocation

The envelope MUST be revocable. The revocation endpoint MUST be reachable for the envelope's declared lifetime. Revocation MUST take effect at the agent's next action, or within a declared maximum revocation latency, whichever is shorter.

5.4 Conformance claim

An implementation conforms to A12 iff every clause in §5.1–§5.3 is satisfied.

---

6. A13 — Counterparty Admission Protocol

6.1 Required contents

A conforming Admission Protocol MUST publish, in machine-readable form:

· (a) The platform's accepted action vocabulary.
· (b) Published error bounds per API (ε_platform).
· (c) Rate limits, cost, and latency guarantees.
· (d) Refusal semantics the platform honors.
· (e) The platform's own hazard inventory.
· (f) Settlement guarantees and reversal windows.

6.2 Symmetry

The protocol MUST apply uniformly to all agents that meet its published terms. A protocol that admits some agents and refuses others on terms not published in the protocol is non-conforming.

6.3 Refusal of admission

The agent MUST refuse admission if ε_platform > the agent's declared tolerance. The agent MUST NOT accept admission to a platform whose published bounds exceed its tolerance.

6.4 Inversion

The publication of the protocol MUST be sufficient to make the admission decision auditable. The decision MUST NOT depend on unpublished terms.

6.5 Conformance claim

An implementation conforms to A13 iff every clause in §6.1–§6.4 is satisfied.

