7. A14 — Action Vocabulary Mapping

7.1 Required artifact

A conforming implementation MUST declare a mapping:

```
f: B_agent → B_platform ∪ {REFUSE}
```

signed, versioned, and inspectable.

7.2 Required guarantees

The mapping MUST guarantee:

· (a) No agent action maps outside the platform's accepted vocabulary.
· (b) No agent composition maps to an unsafe platform composition.

7.3 Compositional verification

Guarantee (b) requires a compositional verification fragment — a decidable subset of system compositions over which the mapping can be proved. The fragment MUST be named.

[BLOCKING — O1] The fragment is not yet named in the inter-organizational paper. Conformance to A14 cannot be assessed until the fragment is specified and its decidability demonstrated.

An implementation MUST NOT claim conformance to A14 while O1 is unresolved.

7.4 No dynamic discovery

The mapping MUST be declared. Dynamic discovery of platform actions at runtime is non-conforming. Runtime scraping is non-conforming.

7.5 Conformance claim

An implementation conforms to A14 iff every clause in §7.1–§7.4 is satisfied and O1 is resolved.

