9. A16 — Cross-Organizational Trace Ledger

9.1 Required contents

A conforming ledger MUST record, for every action:

· (a) The action, its precondition hash, its outcome, and its signature.
· (b) Every refusal, with reason code.
· (c) Every EAR check — observed vs. declared bound.
· (d) Every envelope clause exercised.

9.2 Structural requirements

The ledger MUST be append-only. The ledger MUST be hash-chained. The ledger MUST be Merkle-anchored. The ledger MUST be independently verifiable. Both parties MUST hold a copy.

9.3 Dispute resolution

Disputes MUST resolve against the ledger. A ledger that does not support independent verification is non-conforming. A ledger that permits retroactive modification is non-conforming.

9.4 Retention

The ledger MUST be retained for a declared period, sufficient for the applicable regulatory and liability horizon. The period MUST be declared in the certificate.

9.5 Conformance claim

An implementation conforms to A16 iff every clause in §9.1–§9.4 is satisfied.

