10. The trust root

10.1 Three roles

The Friday session requires three roles:

· Author — proposes the delta.
· Verifier — independently checks the contracts, runs the simulation phase, attempts to falsify the change, signs the verification report.
· Approver — owns the ROM-burn signature, owns the liability, holds veto.

10.2 Non-interchangeability

The roles MUST NOT be interchangeable within a session. A session in which one person holds two roles is non-conforming.

10.3 Liability

The three signers MUST bear liability jointly and severally under a strict-liability regime. A regime in which liability diffuses to "the company" is non-conforming. A regime in which liability attaches only to the Approver is non-conforming.

10.4 Under-three case

If three qualified, independent signers are not available, the session MUST NOT occur. The system MUST remain at its current B*. The refusal code 0x-AMBIG-STAFFING MUST be emitted. A system that continues to burn ROM updates without three signers is non-conforming.

10.5 Veto

The Approver's veto MUST be recorded with a written justification entering the audit log. A veto without a record is non-conforming.

10.6 What this document cannot specify

This document MUST NOT attempt to specify judgment. No clause can require that the Verifier actually attempts falsification, that the Approver actually understands the change, or that the three disagree when they should. This is the boundary of what a standard can do.

