16. Closing note

This document specifies what an implementation MUST do to claim conformance to the inter-organizational layer of AGENTIC ST-T1024.

It names what it cannot yet certify: O1 and O2 are CONFORMANCE BLOCKING. An implementation that claims conformance to A14 or A15 while these blocks are unresolved is non-conforming, and this document says so explicitly. A standard that pretends otherwise is the one to distrust.

Two artifacts remain to be drafted before this document can be circulated as normative:

1. The Agent Certificate schema, as a standalone artifact. This is the most concrete deliverable and the one a counterparty reads first.
2. The compositional verification fragment named in O1. Without it, A14 conformance is undefined.

Until both exist, this document is v0.1 — a proposal about a proposal about a standard.

End of draft.

